WEBVTT

00:46.588 --> 00:49.549
Eun Chae-ni, 27 years old.

00:51.009 --> 00:53.011
A trainwreck of a personality

00:53.511 --> 00:55.221
and a pretty shallow education.

00:58.224 --> 01:00.560
Landing a job is next to impossible…

01:04.773 --> 01:05.899
and to top it all off…

01:15.492 --> 01:17.160
How about another surgery?

01:18.828 --> 01:19.788
Wouldn't that work?

01:19.871 --> 01:21.206
The thing is,

01:21.998 --> 01:25.585
your congestive heart failure
is too advanced.

01:26.961 --> 01:29.589
Your body wouldn't be able to handle it.

01:33.134 --> 01:34.177
So I'm…

01:36.638 --> 01:37.847
really going to die?

01:45.021 --> 01:48.358
A heart that could fail at any moment.

01:51.694 --> 01:54.864
Those who do not believe in God
will be marked by the beast!

01:54.948 --> 01:57.951
And those marked by the beast
will go to hell!

01:58.034 --> 02:00.453
Be saved, everyone!

02:01.496 --> 02:03.289
A life with no escape

02:04.415 --> 02:07.460
that won't change

02:08.044 --> 02:11.548
and has an all too predictable end.

02:13.508 --> 02:14.676
Be saved.

02:16.678 --> 02:18.221
Find salvation.

02:18.304 --> 02:20.140
Find salvation through eternal life.

02:20.640 --> 02:22.142
Don't you wish to be saved?

02:22.642 --> 02:26.354
The apocalypse will happen
on December 31, 1999.

02:26.437 --> 02:28.022
By "the apocalypse,"

02:29.482 --> 02:30.984
do you mean the world will end?

02:31.067 --> 02:32.569
That's right.

02:32.652 --> 02:34.279
But don't you worry.

02:34.362 --> 02:37.574
The blessed will be granted eternal life.

02:39.325 --> 02:42.036
Couldn't it be granted
before Judgment Day?

02:42.120 --> 02:43.329
Sorry?

02:43.413 --> 02:46.916
What about the people who croak
before the apocalypse?

02:47.000 --> 02:51.796
Can't those people be saved in advance?

02:52.297 --> 02:55.425
What, you don't take reservations?

02:55.508 --> 02:57.927
Or maybe move the apocalypse up a little!

02:58.011 --> 03:01.848
Well, there's nothing we can do
about God's will.

03:01.931 --> 03:03.641
What about me, then?

03:03.725 --> 03:05.059
Those who shall be saved…

03:05.143 --> 03:08.188
I want to see the world ending too!

03:08.271 --> 03:11.441
Don't you think it's a raw deal
for me to die without seeing that?

03:11.524 --> 03:13.401
How would I ever rest in peace?

03:14.819 --> 03:15.653
Well?

03:15.737 --> 03:17.405
Have a blessed day.

03:17.488 --> 03:19.824
What, am I asking for too much?

03:19.908 --> 03:22.327
It's not like I'm asking to live forever!

03:23.077 --> 03:28.374
I just want to live long enough to see it!
The end of the world!

03:28.875 --> 03:30.460
I want to see it too!

03:30.543 --> 03:33.087
Show me! I want to see it! Let me see it!

03:33.171 --> 03:35.215
I want to see it!

03:35.298 --> 03:36.716
Let me…

03:49.354 --> 03:52.148
I want to see the entire world…

03:54.525 --> 03:56.069
go up in flames.

03:57.904 --> 03:58.988
How come

04:00.448 --> 04:02.575
I'm not even allowed that?

04:05.203 --> 04:07.830
That's the least I could ask for.

04:24.347 --> 04:26.557
Did you eat a Jaws bar too?

04:34.941 --> 04:35.775
Yeah.

04:36.484 --> 04:37.318
I have now.

04:52.417 --> 04:54.294
Don't cry. Hush.

04:57.964 --> 05:00.466
What if I give you this instead?

05:03.344 --> 05:04.178
Jin-seo!

05:05.388 --> 05:06.848
What are you doing here?

05:07.348 --> 05:09.934
Are you okay?
Mommy has been looking for you.

05:12.979 --> 05:14.939
She's the official trainwreck of Haeseong.

05:15.023 --> 05:17.608
Hey misters,
may you live long, healthy lives.

05:17.692 --> 05:20.903
She's the granddaughter of
the Hearty House owner and a total nutter.

05:20.987 --> 05:22.155
Live long lives, okay?

05:22.238 --> 05:24.073
Best stay away from her, Un-jeong.

05:24.157 --> 05:26.576
-She bites.
-Lucky you, getting to see the apocalypse.

05:26.659 --> 05:27.994
Let's get a move on, people.

05:28.077 --> 05:30.038
-Let's get going.
-How fun!

05:30.538 --> 05:32.749
I swear, this sort of crap is…

05:35.710 --> 05:38.087
What's the point of all this, anyway?

05:38.588 --> 05:42.175
Just go on vacation, everyone! Go travel!

05:42.717 --> 05:44.302
WARNING
THIS IS PRIVATE PROPERTY

05:44.385 --> 05:47.722
TRESPASSING, LITTERING, AND OTHER
ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES ARE PROHIBITED

05:56.230 --> 05:57.231
What's this?

05:58.900 --> 06:00.610
Why, this is perfectly fine.

06:01.944 --> 06:03.363
Do folks have money to burn?

06:11.120 --> 06:13.498
Man, this is really buried deep.

06:18.628 --> 06:20.963
Is someone pulling the darn thing?

06:37.939 --> 06:38.856
What's this?

08:30.801 --> 08:34.472
THE WONDERFOOLS

08:35.681 --> 08:40.311
EPISODE 1
EVERY LIFE COMES WITH A SURPRISE TWIST

08:42.063 --> 08:44.565
I'm pretty sure they're serial murders.

08:50.029 --> 08:54.158
Two weeks ago, Park Yong-sik here
disappeared, and I can't reach him.

08:54.242 --> 08:57.620
Then last week, Kim Bong-pal
also vanished out of the blue.

08:57.703 --> 09:00.289
Maybe you should stop fighting.

09:00.373 --> 09:04.293
No one likes a guy who picks fights
while drunk. I'd cut ties with you too.

09:04.377 --> 09:07.171
I owe Kim Bong-pal 5,000 won.

09:07.255 --> 09:09.674
He'd never cut ties
without getting his money!

09:11.008 --> 09:12.093
Unless he's dead.

09:12.176 --> 09:16.472
Then why don't you file
an official police report?

09:16.556 --> 09:19.350
As if the police would ever listen to me!

09:19.976 --> 09:23.312
Don't you folks say
you listen to the people?

09:23.396 --> 09:25.273
Oh, for God's sake. Where do I--

09:25.356 --> 09:26.566
It's written in the law.

09:26.649 --> 09:30.403
"Article 7, Clause 1. Civil servants
are obliged to serve all citizens…"

09:35.491 --> 09:36.325
Hey, this one.

09:36.409 --> 09:38.411
-This is Kim Na-yeong.
-Stop faking a call.

09:38.494 --> 09:40.663
-Where are you going?
-I don't have a computer.

09:40.746 --> 09:43.916
No, I can't do this.
This is bad. Real bad. Where is he?

09:45.126 --> 09:46.669
Mr. Lee Un-jeong!

09:48.963 --> 09:49.922
This way!

09:50.006 --> 09:51.757
Over here. Right here.

09:51.841 --> 09:52.758
Yes, sir?

09:52.842 --> 09:53.843
Come here.

09:53.926 --> 09:54.760
Right.

09:56.512 --> 09:58.681
You should go. We'll look into it for you.

10:00.808 --> 10:02.018
Why, that…

10:04.395 --> 10:05.980
Oh dear, sorry.

10:06.939 --> 10:08.649
-I'll do it.
-That's okay.

10:09.275 --> 10:12.528
Isn't it about time
for your rite of passage?

10:13.237 --> 10:15.114
He's a regular at our complaints office.

10:21.537 --> 10:23.039
Are you accusing me of lying?

10:23.539 --> 10:25.958
The carp really was
as tall as I am sitting down.

10:26.042 --> 10:28.961
I have a long torso, so seated,
I'm at least 120 centimeters tall!

10:29.045 --> 10:31.547
It was clearly genetically modified!

10:31.631 --> 10:34.592
Someone's been dumping phenol
into the water!

10:34.675 --> 10:37.970
You know V, right?
The show about aliens who eat rats!

10:38.054 --> 10:41.390
It blinked its eyelids sideways,
just like the aliens on that show!

10:41.474 --> 10:43.309
I'm telling you, it's phenol.

10:43.392 --> 10:46.687
Why won't you take my word for it
and go there for an inspection?

10:46.771 --> 10:50.358
Either there's a corpse rotting
somewhere in that reservoir,

10:50.441 --> 10:51.484
or it's phenol!

10:51.984 --> 10:53.736
Just go out there and check!

10:54.487 --> 10:56.447
You have to deal with him

10:56.530 --> 10:58.866
to become a true complaint troubleshooter.

10:58.949 --> 11:02.203
Oddly enough, my stomach's acting up,
so I need the bathroom.

11:02.286 --> 11:03.287
But, sir…

11:07.833 --> 11:09.085
Look at this, will you?

11:09.168 --> 11:12.213
It's a total garbage dump, you know?
You see that?

11:12.296 --> 11:13.506
-Now--
-One moment, sir.

11:19.261 --> 11:20.262
Yes, here.

11:21.514 --> 11:24.934
Our records show
that we already did an inspection

11:25.017 --> 11:27.395
and installed signs
prohibiting illegal dumping.

11:28.396 --> 11:29.355
This thing?

11:29.438 --> 11:31.065
This isn't enough!

11:31.148 --> 11:34.360
Who'd be afraid of a measly sign
that has no legal effect?

11:34.443 --> 11:35.695
-Look.
-One moment, sir.

11:44.620 --> 11:48.207
This land is private property,
so there really isn't anything we can…

11:49.125 --> 11:53.921
Without the owner's consent,
our hands are pretty much tied, sir.

11:58.426 --> 11:59.802
Do my words carry no weight

11:59.885 --> 12:02.847
because I grab a ticket
and patiently wait my turn to see you?

12:03.556 --> 12:05.182
Mr. Lee Un-jeong? Okay.

12:05.266 --> 12:09.770
Should I just go straight to Manager Kim
and get you into trouble?

12:10.271 --> 12:13.774
Or should I go upstairs right now
and take this up with Director Lee?

12:14.358 --> 12:15.192
Well?

12:15.693 --> 12:17.194
Unbelievable.

12:17.903 --> 12:18.738
Honestly!

12:20.740 --> 12:21.866
At Haeseong City Hall,

12:21.949 --> 12:25.202
we have eleven Manager Kims
and four Director Lees.

12:25.786 --> 12:28.914
Which one would you like to speak to, sir?

12:28.998 --> 12:30.166
What's that?

12:33.544 --> 12:37.339
Why, you're one hell of an oddball,
aren't you?

12:51.645 --> 12:52.480
Next, please!

12:52.563 --> 12:54.190
"Next, please"?

13:03.783 --> 13:05.242
You should watch out.

13:07.578 --> 13:11.582
From here, this looks like a quiet
and peaceful rural town, doesn't it?

13:13.584 --> 13:14.919
But it isn't.

13:15.419 --> 13:17.588
If you take a closer look,

13:18.255 --> 13:20.883
there's no place more troubled than this.

13:27.056 --> 13:29.517
People keep disappearing.

13:31.435 --> 13:33.354
Just like 20 years ago.

13:39.777 --> 13:41.111
Last time,

13:42.738 --> 13:47.868
dozens of people,
children and adults alike, went missing.

13:51.413 --> 13:52.873
You'd better be careful.

13:53.457 --> 13:57.127
I figured you wouldn't know,
since you're not from around here.

13:59.922 --> 14:00.840
Yes, sir.

14:02.174 --> 14:03.884
I saw it all.

14:05.177 --> 14:07.930
What happened 20 years ago.

14:47.428 --> 14:48.846
Be saved, sir.

14:51.515 --> 14:54.935
Don't you people have something
better to do? You're such a pain!

14:56.270 --> 14:57.521
Go away!

15:00.232 --> 15:01.233
I said go away!

15:08.991 --> 15:11.035
What is this?

15:11.118 --> 15:14.747
What are you trying to pull?

15:28.844 --> 15:30.095
Believe,

15:31.513 --> 15:33.307
and you shall be saved.

15:39.521 --> 15:40.606
Send me on a trip.

15:42.274 --> 15:43.692
Oh, for crying out loud.

15:45.611 --> 15:47.321
I said I'm going on a trip.

15:47.404 --> 15:48.781
Give me some money!

15:49.281 --> 15:50.115
No.

15:50.199 --> 15:51.992
-Why not?
-Do you really have to ask?

15:52.701 --> 15:55.287
What, are you gonna take your cash
to the afterlife?

15:55.371 --> 15:58.832
You donate hundreds of millions to others,
so why won't you donate to me?

15:58.916 --> 16:01.126
That'd be a waste of money,
not a donation.

16:02.002 --> 16:06.173
Money is only money when you know
how to spend it. Otherwise, it's poison.

16:06.256 --> 16:09.551
We won't know until I've tried spending,
so just give me some!

16:09.635 --> 16:11.345
Let me at least splurge before I die.

16:12.596 --> 16:15.432
Don't you know that death talk
is forbidden in our house?

16:20.771 --> 16:23.315
What is it? Did the doctor say something?

16:26.193 --> 16:29.029
I just mean, what do I have to live for?

16:29.113 --> 16:31.907
I can't go anywhere or do whatever I want!

16:31.991 --> 16:33.993
If you're so unhappy,
then you be my grandma.

16:35.786 --> 16:39.164
Unless you want your pay docked,
cut the crap and go peel some onions.

16:40.791 --> 16:43.794
And don't forget
to take your meds on time, okay?

16:43.877 --> 16:46.463
Do you even know how hard it is
to be your granddaughter?

16:46.547 --> 16:49.842
I don't know about that, but I bet
being your grandma is even harder.

16:54.888 --> 16:58.267
As expected,
Grandma won't give me any money.

17:29.840 --> 17:30.924
KILIMANJARO
AURORA

17:38.057 --> 17:40.642
Okay, let's do it.

17:41.143 --> 17:45.439
I'm gonna visit
at least one place before I die.

18:00.287 --> 18:01.121
Going somewhere?

18:01.205 --> 18:03.207
Yeah, I am. On a trip.

18:04.583 --> 18:07.211
-Your grandma let you?
-Do you think she would?

18:07.294 --> 18:08.337
But what about money?

18:08.420 --> 18:09.755
You'll lend me some.

18:09.838 --> 18:11.048
Right… What?

18:11.548 --> 18:13.092
I can't. I don't have any.

18:13.175 --> 18:15.427
What? Why don't you have any money?

18:15.511 --> 18:17.888
My roof kept leaking.

18:17.971 --> 18:20.182
I had to cash out my savings to fix it.

18:20.265 --> 18:23.393
You're a tenant.
Shouldn't your landlord deal with repairs?

18:23.477 --> 18:25.604
He said he'd fix it next month.

18:25.687 --> 18:29.441
Then you should've waited a month.
Why would you pay? Are you stupid?

18:29.525 --> 18:32.820
Hey, have you ever had to use an umbrella
inside your own home?

18:33.737 --> 18:38.033
You sure live up to your name,
Sappiest Sap of Haeseong.

18:39.535 --> 18:40.828
Anyway, I'm broke.

18:41.745 --> 18:44.123
Anyway, I'm going on a trip.

18:44.206 --> 18:45.582
How exactly?

18:46.500 --> 18:49.920
I see. You have some assets
since you're an heiress and all?

18:50.504 --> 18:52.339
You really are clueless, aren't you?

18:52.422 --> 18:55.050
You have to inherit something
to be an heiress.

18:55.134 --> 18:57.302
-But--
-Who's out there? Eunie?

18:57.386 --> 18:59.096
Did you take your meds?

19:00.889 --> 19:03.559
Which one of us
do you think will live longer?

19:03.642 --> 19:05.561
Take your darn meds!

19:05.644 --> 19:07.396
I already did!

19:09.606 --> 19:11.108
I bet she'll live to 120.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.278
See ya, Sap.

19:14.903 --> 19:15.737
Hey!

19:16.238 --> 19:18.365
How are you gonna travel
without any money?

19:19.241 --> 19:20.409
Don't worry.

19:20.909 --> 19:22.286
This is top secret,

19:24.079 --> 19:27.416
but tomorrow,
I'm due to be 50 million won richer.

19:34.506 --> 19:37.134
So when will it be dealt with?

19:37.217 --> 19:39.136
You know how civil servants are.

19:40.095 --> 19:41.096
A bunch of slowpokes.

19:42.306 --> 19:45.684
I'll try to handle things myself
as swiftly as possible.

19:46.185 --> 19:47.477
But more importantly…

19:49.938 --> 19:52.357
about my mom's 70th birthday trip.

19:53.442 --> 19:55.694
You know we get westerlies
in the summer, right?

19:56.820 --> 19:59.072
Just thinking about how much I suffered

19:59.156 --> 20:01.617
because of the stench
since we had that heavy rain…

20:02.576 --> 20:04.745
-Sales have plummeted too.
-Right.

20:04.828 --> 20:07.998
Who'd want to come
to a flower shop that stinks of rot?

20:08.081 --> 20:10.375
Right, I'll get it dealt with quickly.

20:12.085 --> 20:16.048
Well, once that's done,
my mom's 70th birthday trip…

20:16.548 --> 20:18.425
Why do you keep bringing that up?

20:18.508 --> 20:20.427
I thought we were done talking about it.

20:20.510 --> 20:22.971
You only turn 70 once in your life.

20:23.472 --> 20:25.724
She's never been on a plane before.

20:25.807 --> 20:28.769
Just take her
to the Hawaii resort in Bugok.

20:28.852 --> 20:31.188
The good son act is over in a flash,

20:31.271 --> 20:33.523
but credit card debt lasts a lifetime.

20:34.149 --> 20:34.983
Still--

20:35.067 --> 20:36.193
Yikes, a bug!

20:37.903 --> 20:39.321
Why won't it get off? Why?

20:39.404 --> 20:41.823
Go away! Get off! Oh, I'm so sick of you!

20:41.907 --> 20:44.368
Die, damn it! Die!

20:44.868 --> 20:46.119
Die!

20:47.913 --> 20:51.208
Everything's ready.
Enjoy lunch, Ms. Moon Mi-hui.

20:54.670 --> 20:55.754
It looks pretty dead…

21:01.593 --> 21:03.220
HAESEONG GIRLS' MIDDLE SCHOOL

21:03.303 --> 21:04.429
Seo-yeong, here.

21:04.513 --> 21:06.723
Hey, I'm here. Over here!

21:09.184 --> 21:10.060
Hello?

21:10.143 --> 21:12.312
Hi, Mom. Yeah.

21:13.397 --> 21:14.523
Yes.

21:15.565 --> 21:19.027
Yes, just wait a little longer.
You said it's three months away.

21:19.653 --> 21:20.487
Cheong!

21:28.912 --> 21:29.746
Okay, Mom.

21:31.164 --> 21:32.332
Yes.

21:32.416 --> 21:34.084
Oh, of course.

21:34.584 --> 21:36.211
I'll send you to Hawaii.

21:37.087 --> 21:38.088
Don't you worry.

21:38.588 --> 21:40.465
You know how capable your son is--

21:45.304 --> 21:47.597
Goodness, these shoes…

21:47.681 --> 21:48.682
Mom?

21:49.182 --> 21:50.851
I gotta go. I'll call you later.

21:51.685 --> 21:52.519
Bye.

21:54.187 --> 21:55.731
-Bo-ra, let's go together.
-Sure.

21:56.315 --> 21:58.817
-Want to go get tteokbokki?
-That sounds great.

21:58.900 --> 22:00.485
-Okay!
-Should we skip cram school?

22:00.569 --> 22:02.321
Sweet, sounds good!

22:02.404 --> 22:03.238
Let's go.

22:03.947 --> 22:05.449
My shoes are soaked.

22:14.041 --> 22:16.043
Wow, 50 million won.

22:16.752 --> 22:18.462
I'm so jealous.

22:35.062 --> 22:37.230
There's nothing to steal.
Why lock the door?

22:37.314 --> 22:39.274
It's to keep things out.

22:39.775 --> 22:41.735
Like bugs, cats…

22:42.986 --> 22:43.862
Especially you.

22:49.785 --> 22:52.496
Hey, why'd you shut the door in my face?

22:53.205 --> 22:54.831
Oh no!

23:00.462 --> 23:02.255
Hey, there.

23:05.634 --> 23:07.219
Didn't you say you got it fixed?

23:08.845 --> 23:10.222
I did.

23:11.807 --> 23:14.726
I paid a lot of money for it too.

23:14.810 --> 23:16.812
Are you laughing or crying?

24:50.947 --> 24:52.866
Chae-ni, are you going somewhere?

24:52.949 --> 24:54.701
And your grandma actually let you?

24:54.784 --> 24:56.703
Well, Chae-ni, you sure are lucky.

24:56.786 --> 24:59.623
-What's gotten into the Hearty House lady?
-Exactly.

24:59.706 --> 25:02.083
Chae-ni, aren't you lucky?
Have a great trip!

25:02.167 --> 25:04.669
-Is Chae-ni going somewhere?
-I think she's traveling.

25:05.170 --> 25:08.215
Always best to travel
while your knees are still good!

25:39.538 --> 25:40.539
What?

25:41.456 --> 25:42.666
What the heck?

25:45.627 --> 25:46.795
Damn it.

25:55.178 --> 25:56.388
It's Mr. Kim's.

25:57.514 --> 25:59.516
Where did he go without his cart?

26:00.850 --> 26:02.310
I'll bring it back soon.

26:19.286 --> 26:21.580
Isn't this Mr. Kim Bong-pal's cart?

26:23.498 --> 26:24.332
Who are you?

26:26.668 --> 26:28.503
Are you the new supermarket manager?

26:32.632 --> 26:33.675
Fine, take it.

26:33.758 --> 26:35.468
Take it. It's all yours.

26:56.865 --> 26:59.284
I'm pretty sure they're serial murders.

27:00.285 --> 27:02.454
She's the official trainwreck of Haeseong.

27:02.537 --> 27:03.747
Best stay away from her.

27:03.830 --> 27:05.373
You'd better be careful.

27:05.457 --> 27:07.626
People keep disappearing.

27:11.546 --> 27:12.756
What are you doing?

27:13.923 --> 27:15.258
That's a pretty big suitcase.

27:15.967 --> 27:17.469
What's it to you?

27:19.804 --> 27:21.806
Where is Mr. Kim Bong-pal?

27:22.932 --> 27:24.267
How would I know?

27:25.352 --> 27:27.646
May I check your suitcase?

27:27.729 --> 27:28.938
What do you have in here?

27:29.022 --> 27:32.776
Whatever I wanted to put in there!
What do you want with my suitcase?

27:35.445 --> 27:36.279
What the…

27:38.114 --> 27:38.990
What the heck?

27:40.784 --> 27:42.118
Let go!

28:36.047 --> 28:37.257
I'll…

28:49.144 --> 28:50.395
I think there's been a--

29:06.619 --> 29:07.495
Hello?

29:07.996 --> 29:10.540
Being out in the rain
won't do you any good.

29:10.623 --> 29:11.958
Where'd you go?

29:12.542 --> 29:13.543
I just

29:14.252 --> 29:15.962
had to take care of something.

29:16.045 --> 29:17.088
Take care of what?

29:17.589 --> 29:20.467
What could you possibly have
to take care of in the rain?

29:21.301 --> 29:22.552
Where are you?

29:23.595 --> 29:24.554
Hey, say…

29:24.637 --> 29:25.722
Hello?

29:27.015 --> 29:27.849
Hello?

29:28.349 --> 29:29.476
-Hello?
-Grandma, hold on.

29:37.025 --> 29:38.109
Your contact info.

29:50.288 --> 29:52.123
JUNIOR OFFICIAL LEE UN-JEONG

29:53.917 --> 29:55.418
Haeseong City Hall Complaints?

29:55.502 --> 29:56.920
Haeseong City Hall Complaints?

29:57.003 --> 29:59.506
Why? Did someone
file a complaint against you?

29:59.589 --> 30:01.299
What did you do this time?

30:01.382 --> 30:04.135
My lawyer will be in touch, so hang tight.

30:04.636 --> 30:06.679
Dry cleaning money won't cut it.

30:07.639 --> 30:08.473
Okay.

30:13.561 --> 30:14.437
Goodbye, then.

30:22.737 --> 30:25.532
It's nothing, Grandma. But why'd you call?

30:25.615 --> 30:27.200
Why do you think?

30:27.283 --> 30:29.327
What if you catch a cold? Hurry home.

30:30.119 --> 30:32.956
I told you not to go out
when the weather changes.

30:34.415 --> 30:35.708
Grandma.

30:37.919 --> 30:40.296
Can't you just let me go on a trip?

30:41.923 --> 30:43.716
There you go again with that nonsense.

30:45.635 --> 30:48.471
How could you travel in your condition?

30:49.931 --> 30:54.811
Is living a long life
all that you want for me?

30:55.395 --> 30:58.439
Incapable of doing anything,
just wasting away?

31:00.108 --> 31:02.193
Doesn't it frustrate you
to see me like this?

31:02.277 --> 31:04.195
Aren't you embarrassed
to face the neighbors?

31:05.321 --> 31:06.322
I'm not.

31:07.532 --> 31:08.825
Why would I be embarrassed?

31:10.285 --> 31:11.870
I'm just waiting.

31:13.371 --> 31:16.207
What, you think you were healthy as a kid?

31:17.792 --> 31:18.960
But still,

31:20.128 --> 31:21.462
you were ever so kind,

31:21.963 --> 31:23.256
well-mannered,

31:23.965 --> 31:25.383
and always gave your best.

31:27.552 --> 31:29.012
You were such a darling.

31:29.971 --> 31:33.474
You weren't good at anything,
but you were still such a darling.

31:34.100 --> 31:36.185
Because you powered through and lived on.

31:38.938 --> 31:43.902
I'm waiting for the day when that darling
Eun Chae-ni hiding deep inside of you

31:45.653 --> 31:47.697
crawls her way out.

31:52.744 --> 31:53.912
Well, don't.

31:54.621 --> 31:56.122
She died a long time ago.

31:56.205 --> 31:57.957
Eunie, you really…

31:58.458 --> 32:00.793
I told you not to talk about dying.

32:01.461 --> 32:03.838
I told you
that's off-limits in this house!

32:06.049 --> 32:07.467
The thing is, Grandma,

32:08.635 --> 32:10.178
I really am going to die.

32:23.733 --> 32:27.403
But I never imagined I'd die like this.

32:30.740 --> 32:35.119
Without you by my side
and in front of these guys, no less.

32:45.755 --> 32:47.465
Now, this is a plot twist.

32:47.548 --> 32:51.678
So you wasted two million
on waterproof paint for the roof?

32:51.761 --> 32:53.179
Shame on you.

32:53.262 --> 32:55.390
I knew you weren't just any old sap.

32:55.473 --> 32:58.685
You deserve to be called
the sappiest of all saps.

33:03.481 --> 33:06.192
I wish money would just fall
from the sky--

33:09.404 --> 33:11.114
If only there were cash lying around.

33:11.990 --> 33:13.449
Why's it taking so long to boil?

33:15.118 --> 33:18.621
Nothing in life goes my goddamn way.

33:19.205 --> 33:21.708
Yet some people are going on vacation
with 50 million.

33:21.791 --> 33:23.418
Who is?

33:23.501 --> 33:26.045
Who has 50 million to blow on a vacation?

33:26.129 --> 33:28.923
Who else would I know
who has that much money?

33:29.007 --> 33:31.509
There's no way
the Hearty House owner would travel.

33:32.927 --> 33:36.055
Her granddaughter?
Eun Chae-ni, Lady Trainwreck?

33:40.226 --> 33:41.060
Begone!

33:42.395 --> 33:44.147
Did you just call me a trainwreck?

33:44.897 --> 33:48.234
Yeah. What's wrong with calling
a trainwreck a trainwreck?

33:48.901 --> 33:49.736
Touché.

33:50.862 --> 33:52.447
You're right, Mr. Royal Nightmare.

33:52.530 --> 33:53.448
What, Nightmare?

33:53.531 --> 33:55.450
Watch what you call your elders, you brat.

33:55.533 --> 33:57.910
What's wrong with calling
a nightmare a nightmare?

33:58.494 --> 34:00.038
-Why, you little brat--
-Stop.

34:00.121 --> 34:01.706
Come on, Chae-ni.

34:01.789 --> 34:04.000
Mr. Son, you too.
Easy with that stink eye.

34:04.083 --> 34:06.544
Stay out of this, Sappy Sap of Haeseong.

34:06.627 --> 34:08.337
Yeah, butt out, Sappy Sap.

34:08.421 --> 34:10.798
Hey, I asked you not to call me that.

34:10.882 --> 34:13.009
It makes me feel left out.

34:13.092 --> 34:15.553
You guys are the only ones
who get cool nicknames.

34:16.137 --> 34:18.556
Can't you give me a cool nickname
like "King Sap"?

34:18.639 --> 34:21.434
King Sap sounds like
a pretty powerful sap, at least.

34:21.517 --> 34:22.977
You think anyone can be a royal?

34:23.061 --> 34:24.187
Of course not.

34:24.270 --> 34:27.440
You need to build up a bad rep for years,
constantly pick fights,

34:27.523 --> 34:29.609
and have the tenacity and perseverance

34:29.692 --> 34:33.154
to not give a hoot about others
in order to be crowned a royal.

34:33.738 --> 34:34.781
Give me a break.

34:34.864 --> 34:37.158
I'd expect no less
from Haeseong's Royal Nightmare.

34:37.742 --> 34:39.410
Someone's brimming with pride.

34:39.494 --> 34:42.163
I heard you were going on
a 50-million-won trip,

34:42.246 --> 34:44.582
but I guess you sent your manners
on the road early.

34:44.665 --> 34:47.710
Did your manners
take your sense of respect with them?

34:47.794 --> 34:49.712
Too bad. Will you even be able to go?

34:49.796 --> 34:53.049
How could you leave Haeseong
when everyone knows your grandma?

34:53.132 --> 34:56.219
Man, I almost want to rat you out.

34:57.261 --> 34:58.304
That's why

34:59.514 --> 35:01.641
the Royal Nightmare and Sappy Sap

35:02.558 --> 35:03.392
need to help me.

35:03.476 --> 35:06.562
You think I'd help a kid
who calls her elder a "nightmare"?

35:06.646 --> 35:09.148
I'll compensate you generously.
Five million each.

35:09.232 --> 35:11.901
What should we do first, m'lady?

35:13.069 --> 35:14.987
First, I should bring in my luggage.

35:15.071 --> 35:17.281
Please, leave it to me,
your humble servant.

35:17.782 --> 35:19.367
We're already on it, ma'am.

35:22.912 --> 35:25.206
What did I possibly do that was so wrong?

35:26.290 --> 35:28.126
Where did it all go south?

35:29.877 --> 35:32.713
I forgot that the world
is disgustingly unfair.

35:32.797 --> 35:36.551
Right. They say worrying about an heiress
is the greatest waste of time.

35:42.431 --> 35:44.684
Did I dig my own grave?

35:49.063 --> 35:51.858
The people downstairs complained
about the noise again.

35:51.941 --> 35:53.734
What are you up to every night?

35:54.652 --> 35:56.237
Didn't you say you lived alone?

35:56.779 --> 35:59.448
Why are you thumping away
every night by yourself?

36:00.032 --> 36:02.118
I'm sorry. I'll be more careful.

36:02.201 --> 36:04.579
I told you it's an old building
with thin walls.

36:04.662 --> 36:06.372
Please be more mindful.

37:02.762 --> 37:04.472
ILLEGAL DUMPING IN HAEDEUL-RI HILL

37:04.555 --> 37:06.015
COMPLAINT REPORT

37:30.873 --> 37:31.707
Yes?

37:36.462 --> 37:38.923
I told you I'd be the one to contact you.

37:42.343 --> 37:44.553
You don't have to keep checking up on me.

37:45.221 --> 37:46.555
It's being dealt with.

38:27.763 --> 38:29.348
NUMBER 2415
STATUS: DORMANT

38:38.065 --> 38:39.650
HA WON-DO

38:42.903 --> 38:44.530
CHOI YEONG-JUN

38:46.407 --> 38:48.909
DR. HA WON-DO WINS GERMANY'S
SCIENTIST OF THE YEAR AWARD

38:48.993 --> 38:50.953
CLAIMED TO SAVE HUMANITY, ONLY LEFT SCARS

38:51.037 --> 38:52.538
EXPLOSION AT ORPHANAGE

38:54.498 --> 38:55.666
POLITICIAN CONDEMNS DR. HA

38:55.750 --> 38:57.376
IMMORAL BIOLOGICAL EXPERIMENTS

38:57.460 --> 38:59.211
THE SWEET HOME WELFARE CENTER TRAGEDY

39:08.137 --> 39:12.433
UNVEILING THE HORRIFYING TRUTH
HAWONDO LAB'S SECURITY GUARD TELLS ALL

40:08.322 --> 40:10.366
APOCALYPSE ON DECEMBER 31ST
SEEK SALVATION

40:12.827 --> 40:14.370
CHURCH OF ETERNAL SALVATION

40:14.453 --> 40:17.164
13 HAEDEUL-RI, HAEJEON-EUP, HAESEONG-SI

41:09.049 --> 41:09.925
What…

41:23.564 --> 41:24.607
What's that?

41:37.786 --> 41:39.246
Kim Bong-pal?

41:40.289 --> 41:41.290
In what ways

41:42.208 --> 41:43.876
can money change a person,

41:43.959 --> 41:46.504
and how far can it transform them?

41:57.515 --> 41:58.891
Grandma.

42:00.392 --> 42:01.727
If you just pay them,

42:02.937 --> 42:04.647
I think this'll all be over soon.

42:06.941 --> 42:07.775
All they want

42:09.610 --> 42:10.778
is five big ones.

42:13.364 --> 42:14.490
Five.

42:17.201 --> 42:18.369
If you just pay them…

42:19.370 --> 42:21.413
Is it really okay for us to do this?

42:21.956 --> 42:25.876
Do I look like I'm enjoying this?
Aren't you tired of being called a sap?

42:28.087 --> 42:31.090
Just shut it,
and let's get this over with.

42:33.384 --> 42:34.218
Hey.

42:38.847 --> 42:39.682
Oh no.

42:41.767 --> 42:42.685
Hey…

42:42.768 --> 42:44.186
It's beating too fast.

42:49.650 --> 42:50.651
Why did you do that?

42:50.734 --> 42:51.569
I

42:53.153 --> 42:56.448
really wanted to climb Kilimanjaro.

42:56.949 --> 42:58.659
Or at least see the northern lights.

43:19.013 --> 43:21.181
Grandma…

43:38.240 --> 43:41.410
Hey, I think we can do better.
Let's do one more take.

43:42.202 --> 43:44.622
Okay, three, two…

43:45.122 --> 43:45.956
Action.

43:57.384 --> 43:58.218
Chae-ni.

43:59.595 --> 44:00.679
Chae-ni?

44:00.763 --> 44:01.972
What's wrong with her?

44:02.473 --> 44:03.390
Chae-ni.

44:28.791 --> 44:29.625
Delete that.

44:29.708 --> 44:31.168
What? Why?

44:31.251 --> 44:32.419
Delete it.

44:47.559 --> 44:50.229
What is it?

44:50.938 --> 44:52.815
What's wrong with Chae-ni?

44:53.440 --> 44:55.442
And what's wrong with you?

44:56.235 --> 44:57.152
Chae-ni…

44:59.988 --> 45:01.323
is dead.

45:09.915 --> 45:11.792
INCOMING CALL

45:15.587 --> 45:19.883
At 9:27 p.m.
on a certain day and month in 1999,

45:21.135 --> 45:22.428
ridiculous as it is,

45:23.011 --> 45:24.179
I really

45:25.973 --> 45:27.599
died just like this.

45:29.101 --> 45:31.937
She better not be off somewhere
causing trouble again.

45:33.313 --> 45:37.401
Thanks to you, Eunie,
my life is so full of thrills.

45:39.862 --> 45:41.447
PRIVATE INVESTIGATOR, GU JUN-MO

45:50.122 --> 45:52.416
COLD CASES

45:52.499 --> 45:54.418
URBAN LEGENDS OF HAESEONG

46:00.716 --> 46:02.092
Yes, this is Gu Jun-mo.

46:02.176 --> 46:05.304
Hey, Jun-mo. I need you to do me a favor.

46:07.139 --> 46:08.140
What is it?

46:08.640 --> 46:10.267
Is Eun Chae-ni not answering again?

46:10.350 --> 46:13.437
Since you know, I'll just get to it.
Go ahead and track her.

46:13.520 --> 46:16.940
Why bother paying for that again?
She'll come home when it's time.

46:17.024 --> 46:18.150
Tell me about it.

46:18.650 --> 46:21.487
You could have done it for free
if you were still a cop.

46:21.570 --> 46:22.988
Why quit and make me pay?

46:23.071 --> 46:25.115
I'll look into it right away, ma'am.

46:36.960 --> 46:40.422
Chae-ni, I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

46:41.089 --> 46:44.510
Don't die. Please don't die.

46:51.642 --> 46:52.768
I can't believe this.

46:53.268 --> 46:54.645
How is this possible?

46:55.354 --> 46:58.565
We didn't even lay a finger on her,
so how could she just die?

46:59.775 --> 47:01.318
Who's going to believe this?

47:01.819 --> 47:03.070
And on top of that,

47:04.780 --> 47:06.532
we're her kidnappers right now.

47:11.119 --> 47:14.498
Mr. Son, what are you doing?
I told you to call an ambulance!

47:15.999 --> 47:17.084
It's too late.

47:17.167 --> 47:21.129
Just call them already.
At this rate, we'll really lose Chae-ni!

47:21.213 --> 47:23.799
She's already dead!

47:24.299 --> 47:25.509
Her pupils are…

47:26.009 --> 47:29.888
Her pupils are dilated.

47:36.228 --> 47:38.564
Poor Chae-ni.

47:39.439 --> 47:41.358
What about her poor grandma?

47:42.109 --> 47:44.027
And what about us?

47:52.077 --> 47:54.454
-For now, we hide her.
-What?

47:55.205 --> 47:59.251
One wrong move, and we'll both be charged
with kidnapping and murder.

48:01.295 --> 48:03.505
Still, that doesn't seem right.

48:04.006 --> 48:04.840
If we just

48:05.716 --> 48:08.051
explain that she died because of us--

48:08.135 --> 48:10.596
And who would believe that

48:10.679 --> 48:12.973
when the mastermind up and died?

48:13.056 --> 48:15.475
Then what do we do now?

48:15.559 --> 48:17.311
That's why I'm saying we dump her.

48:19.187 --> 48:20.314
No, I mean…

48:22.232 --> 48:25.986
Chae-ni isn't trash!
How could we just dump her?

48:26.486 --> 48:29.072
Chae-ni is my friend!

48:29.156 --> 48:33.994
No, I don't mean dump her.
I meant that we should hide her.

48:34.494 --> 48:36.872
We'll just lay her to rest temporarily.

48:41.251 --> 48:43.545
Why…

48:44.504 --> 48:45.881
Chae-ni.

48:46.965 --> 48:49.635
Please close your eyes.

48:50.218 --> 48:53.263
Holy smokes, I'm so scared.

48:53.764 --> 48:56.016
Please just close your eyes.

49:00.187 --> 49:03.231
Chae-ni, I'm sorry. Close your eyes…

49:05.567 --> 49:06.610
I'm so scared.

49:09.529 --> 49:10.530
I'm freaking out!

49:12.866 --> 49:13.951
That's right.

49:14.451 --> 49:18.205
The one who orchestrated this kidnapping
that hastened my death

49:18.747 --> 49:19.915
was me, Eun Chae-ni.

49:20.499 --> 49:22.918
You guys are so frustrating, seriously.

49:23.001 --> 49:26.922
You both wear masks, and one of you films
while the other appears on camera with me.

49:27.005 --> 49:29.257
That's all you have to do.
What's the fuss?

49:29.341 --> 49:30.842
That was the 50 million won

49:31.510 --> 49:33.011
you said you'd be getting?

49:33.512 --> 49:34.346
Oh, come on!

49:35.013 --> 49:37.599
I'll receive the money
and give you your shares.

49:37.683 --> 49:39.851
There's no way we'll get caught.

49:39.935 --> 49:41.269
Don't you know I'm smart?

49:41.770 --> 49:43.397
If you can't trust me,

49:43.939 --> 49:44.856
trust my brain.

49:44.940 --> 49:49.444
Isn't it unfair if you get 50 million,
and we only get 5 million won apiece?

49:49.528 --> 49:50.988
Then count yourself out.

49:51.071 --> 49:53.031
Do you want to film or should I?

49:53.115 --> 49:54.658
Seriously?

49:55.409 --> 49:57.995
I'd feel so guilty toward your grandma.

49:58.078 --> 50:00.831
How could we stab her
in the back like this?

50:00.914 --> 50:02.791
Why don't you think it through again?

50:04.167 --> 50:07.170
I'm sure you've built up
more than just debt against Grandma.

50:09.464 --> 50:10.841
Think about it.

50:10.924 --> 50:12.968
All those years of Grandma's bullying.

50:17.222 --> 50:21.059
But why now?
Why do you suddenly want to go on a trip?

50:22.394 --> 50:23.228
Just because.

50:23.729 --> 50:27.107
If I don't go now,
I don't think I'll ever get to go.

50:28.358 --> 50:31.361
That's true.
You'd never earn enough peeling onions.

50:31.445 --> 50:34.156
But still, isn't this a little too…

50:34.239 --> 50:37.117
I'm worried about both your heart
and your grandma.

50:37.200 --> 50:41.580
I left her a letter.
She'll understand once she reads it.

50:42.664 --> 50:44.916
Just help me out, will you?

50:45.584 --> 50:47.961
I'm really excited right now.

50:49.421 --> 50:51.840
I haven't felt this alive in a long time.

51:10.776 --> 51:12.944
Are you sure
you're not just pretending to push?

51:14.780 --> 51:17.783
This is me pushing with all my strength.

51:18.283 --> 51:19.326
So,

51:20.327 --> 51:21.745
where are we gonna dump her?

51:21.828 --> 51:25.332
We're not dumping her. This is temporary!
Temporarily laying her to rest.

51:25.415 --> 51:28.585
Exactly. Where are we gonna dump Chae-ni…

51:31.963 --> 51:32.839
Chae-ni.

51:34.716 --> 51:37.219
Mr. Son, Chae-ni won't close her eyes.

51:45.519 --> 51:46.603
We're here.

51:47.813 --> 51:48.647
This is it.

51:50.315 --> 51:51.900
People rarely come here,

51:52.609 --> 51:54.069
and there are no cameras.

51:54.569 --> 51:56.988
A place the authorities will never look,

51:57.072 --> 51:59.282
abandoned even by its landowner.

51:59.825 --> 52:01.368
A land of tragedy.

52:01.868 --> 52:06.623
Mr. Son, are you sure
we really have to go this far?

52:11.086 --> 52:13.547
Just until we come up with alibis, okay?

52:14.256 --> 52:15.841
Chae-ni will understand.

52:16.341 --> 52:20.053
She wouldn't like it if we were blamed
for something she planned.

52:21.138 --> 52:22.097
Got it?

52:23.557 --> 52:24.391
Let's go.

52:29.146 --> 52:29.980
Be gentle.

52:35.861 --> 52:36.903
Let's switch.

52:46.746 --> 52:47.581
Lift her.

52:52.419 --> 52:53.920
Careful on the way down.

52:54.629 --> 52:55.797
Okay.

52:56.298 --> 52:57.174
All right.

52:57.924 --> 52:59.301
One, two…

52:59.885 --> 53:01.094
Excuse me.

53:13.398 --> 53:14.357
Mr. Son Gyeong-hun?

53:14.441 --> 53:15.358
Yes.

53:19.696 --> 53:21.031
What are you doing here?

53:23.366 --> 53:26.036
You raise daily complaints
about dumping on these grounds,

53:26.119 --> 53:27.746
then dump trash here yourself?

53:30.749 --> 53:33.335
The oddball from City Hall?

53:34.252 --> 53:35.170
Why are you here?

53:35.253 --> 53:37.923
Because someone grumbled
that we weren't doing inspections.

53:38.006 --> 53:40.091
You said it'd be no use even if you did.

53:41.343 --> 53:45.305
That you were stuck without the landowner.
Oh, whatever. Just go.

53:45.388 --> 53:47.140
I'm withdrawing my complaint. Withdrawn.

53:53.772 --> 53:54.606
What's that…

53:56.900 --> 53:57.817
behind you?

54:04.491 --> 54:05.492
What…

54:36.648 --> 54:37.565
What

54:38.984 --> 54:39.943
is that?

54:50.245 --> 54:51.246
A mannequin.

54:52.455 --> 54:53.832
You expect me to believe that?

55:34.122 --> 55:35.457
We didn't kill her!

56:05.904 --> 56:07.238
The two of you…

56:07.739 --> 56:09.657
Were you trying to dispose of a dead body?

56:10.241 --> 56:11.993
Dispose of a body? No, that's not…

56:12.077 --> 56:13.119
We…

56:14.788 --> 56:16.414
You see, we…

56:16.498 --> 56:18.792
At first, we were just pretending
to kidnap her--

56:18.875 --> 56:20.210
A kidnapping and murder?

56:20.293 --> 56:22.837
No, we didn't!

56:23.380 --> 56:25.090
I swear we didn't even touch her.

56:25.882 --> 56:28.134
She just died on her own.

56:28.718 --> 56:30.804
Chae-ni!

56:31.971 --> 56:34.933
Do you think we wanted to do this?

56:35.016 --> 56:37.018
She's our neighbor!

56:38.186 --> 56:42.690
We even know the old lady
who runs Hearty House.

56:42.774 --> 56:45.193
Do you really think we wanted to do this?

56:45.860 --> 56:47.570
By Hearty House, do you mean…

56:48.154 --> 56:50.573
You mean that so-called trainwreck, right?

56:50.657 --> 56:51.616
Yes.

56:52.700 --> 56:54.828
Chae-ni!

56:57.497 --> 56:59.749
Chae-ni!

57:00.500 --> 57:02.836
Chae-ni! Chae…

57:05.755 --> 57:06.589
Chae-ni?

57:07.674 --> 57:09.175
Chae-ni, where did she go?

57:09.259 --> 57:11.052
-Mr. Son, where'd she go?
-Where is she?

57:11.136 --> 57:12.762
Where is she? She was right here.

57:13.388 --> 57:15.682
-Chae-ni. Where?
-Go check over there.

57:17.600 --> 57:18.768
-Chae-ni.
-Chae-ni!

57:18.852 --> 57:20.145
Chae-ni!

57:20.228 --> 57:21.521
-Chae-ni!
-Chae-ni?

57:21.604 --> 57:23.648
-Chae-ni.
-Chae-ni!

57:24.149 --> 57:26.568
Chae-ni.

57:26.651 --> 57:29.571
What's going on here?
Do you have another accomplice?

57:30.155 --> 57:32.490
-No!
-No!

57:32.574 --> 57:35.076
Then where did the body go?
What did you do with it?

57:35.994 --> 57:37.078
Is there someone else?

57:37.912 --> 57:39.581
No, there isn't!

57:40.582 --> 57:42.834
We really didn't do it.

57:43.418 --> 57:47.797
But given the circumstances,
anyone would think that we did it,

57:48.298 --> 57:52.177
so we were just going
to leave her here temporarily.

57:54.304 --> 57:56.556
If you don't tell me,
I'm calling the cops.

57:56.639 --> 57:58.641
-Sir, please.
-Where's your accomplice?

57:59.851 --> 58:00.768
I'll do it.

58:00.852 --> 58:02.937
Mr. Oddball! Just a second.

58:04.606 --> 58:06.483
Just hear me out for a…

58:06.566 --> 58:07.484
Mr. Oddball!

58:08.735 --> 58:09.986
Let go!

58:13.281 --> 58:14.782
No, please.

58:14.866 --> 58:15.742
Let go!

58:16.242 --> 58:19.162
-Let go of me!
-Mr. Oddball, sir.

58:19.245 --> 58:20.955
Sir Oddball, please!

58:22.415 --> 58:24.250
You can't call the cops!

58:24.876 --> 58:26.794
She really did die on her own.

58:27.420 --> 58:29.589
But if you report it
as a kidnapping and murder,

58:29.672 --> 58:31.508
we'll definitely be charged

58:31.591 --> 58:34.010
as the culprits!

58:34.802 --> 58:36.846
Hello?

58:36.930 --> 58:39.766
Hello? Did I just hear you say
a kidnapping and murder?

58:42.477 --> 58:44.020
No!

58:44.103 --> 58:45.980
That's not it!

58:46.064 --> 58:47.815
We're innocent!

59:07.418 --> 59:10.255
This is 112.
We traced your number due to the urgency.

59:10.338 --> 59:13.299
Where are you right now, sir?
Are you safe?

59:14.217 --> 59:15.718
Is this Mr. Lee Un-jeong?

59:16.219 --> 59:17.804
What's the situation right now?

59:19.764 --> 59:23.518
A squad car has been dispatched,
so please hang in there.

59:23.601 --> 59:25.186
A car has been dispatched!

59:25.979 --> 59:28.731
We're done for!

59:29.691 --> 59:32.026
Oh no!

59:32.694 --> 59:34.070
No!

59:36.447 --> 59:43.454
HEARTY HOUSE

59:49.752 --> 59:51.421
-Get out of there.
-I can't.

59:51.504 --> 59:53.256
-Hey, just a moment.
-What's your name?

59:53.339 --> 59:54.591
Don't come closer.

59:54.674 --> 59:56.676
I need your name, sir.

59:57.677 --> 59:59.262
-Get over here.
-Seriously?

59:59.345 --> 01:00:00.763
Just stay right here, then.

01:00:01.931 --> 01:00:03.433
God, it stinks.

01:00:04.726 --> 01:00:06.853
Wait, time out!

01:00:07.645 --> 01:00:09.772
-Mr. Lee Un-jeong, you called it in?
-Yes.

01:00:09.856 --> 01:00:11.232
I told you I didn't do it.

01:00:11.316 --> 01:00:15.528
I witnessed those two men
trying to dispose of a woman's dead body.

01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:19.240
So where's the body?

01:00:19.824 --> 01:00:22.994
I think their accomplice hid it
while they distracted me.

01:00:23.077 --> 01:00:24.370
It disappeared.

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:29.917
And the victim was
Ms. Eun Chae-ni of Hearty House?

01:00:31.044 --> 01:00:31.878
Yes.

01:00:32.503 --> 01:00:33.546
I believe so.

01:00:33.630 --> 01:00:35.798
Are you talking about that woman
over there?

01:00:38.593 --> 01:00:40.553
Yes, that's right.

01:00:58.196 --> 01:01:00.031
Isn't that Chae-ni?

01:01:21.886 --> 01:01:22.720
I…

01:01:24.514 --> 01:01:25.390
That woman…

01:01:26.933 --> 01:01:28.726
was definitely dead.

01:01:55.002 --> 01:01:56.504
Let go!

01:06:08.339 --> 01:06:13.344
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
